# Cap dome: a plain round mushroom cap, form only, 3.2 m across and 1.1 m tall, its flat underside at the origin. The model using it
# wraps it in a material, so the same form is an amanita's red, a porcini's brown or a honey fungus's amber. Used scaled and tilted
# in the cap masses (fungi/clusters), where it merges with the others, so it has no gills.
format 1

Intersection
    Ellipsoid radii=(1.6, 1.1, 1.6)
    Translate translation=(0, 1.1, 0)
        Box size=(4, 1.1, 4)
